# KIT-CLASS: KIT — the design module's manifest. Every line is `<key>: <value>`; process/MODULES.md says what each key takes. See process/EXTRACTION.md.
name: design
version: 0.4.0
purpose: Evergreen screen designs beside the PRDs: the rules for where they live and how a story and a card cite them, and a Designer role to keep them true.
release-notes: RELEASE-NOTES.md
requires: python3 | python3 -c 'import sys; sys.exit(0 if sys.version_info >= (3, 9) else 1)' | install Python 3.9 or later from your system's packages | required
requires: node | node -e 'process.exit(parseInt(process.versions.node) >= 22 ? 0 : 1)' | install Node 22 or later (nodejs.org or your system's packages) | optional: the token generator m3-tokens.mjs
requires: chrome | for c in google-chrome google-chrome-stable chromium chromium-browser chrome "${CHROME:-}"; do [ -n "$c" ] && command -v "$c" >/dev/null 2>&1 && exit 0; done; [ -x '/Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome' ] | install Google Chrome or Chromium | optional: render.py draws no board without it
role: Designer   authors the screens on the canvas with the artifact tools, takes them into the repo, and keeps the design record true; commits as [Designer]
